tic path through such nodes is nearly guaranteed by hub degree alone and carries essentially no evidence of influence transfer.\n- **Decisive point:** each required link fires exactly **once** over the 100k horizon \u2014 1385\u2192595 (1 event), 595\u2192528 (1 event), 528\u21921186 (1 event) (steps 13, 14, 12). There is no repeated contact to give the chain multiple chances to align. With a 600-unit relay bound inside a 38,399-unit query window, the chance that two independent single-shot edges happen to land in the right order within \u0394 is ~0.1% (step_16). The graph-wide repeat ratio of 0.053 (step_01) confirms this is a near-simple graph where such coincidences are not systematically manufactured.\n\nSince the path rests on single-occurrence edges through generic hubs, the connection is best explained by hub popularity and time-ignoring reachability \u2014 exactly the explanations the task flags as insufficient.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_20982933\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1385, 1186, 595, 528, 639, 1688],\n  \"window\": [61549, 99948],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1385 and 1186 are both sparse nodes (11 and 9 events, no repeats). A static directed route exists (1385->595->528->1186, plus variants via 639/1688), but every relay is a top-15 global hub (595: 418 events/296 partners; 639: 486; 1688: 375; 528: 182), so time-ignoring reachability here is an artifact of hub degree rather than evidence of influence. Critically, each required link occurs exactly once across the full 100k horizon, giving the chain a single chance to satisfy the 600-unit relay bound; the expected number of such aligned 2-hop chains in the 38,399-unit window is ~0.001. I therefore judge no genuine time-respecting cascade from 1385 to 1186. Caveat: the available tools expose only whole-horizon aggregates and never raw timestamps, so the ordering of the three specific events could not be read off directly; the verdict rests on single-occurrence edges plus the hub confound, which is why confidence is moderate rather than high.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 43882, "total_output_tokens": 5669, "total_tokens": 49551, "total_latency_ms": 85567, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}